<title>USA: USDA releases $120 Mln in export credits to Turkey.</title>
<headline>USDA releases $120 Mln in export credits to Turkey.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday it released an additional $120 million in short-term GSM-102 export credits to Turkey to facilitate U.S. ag exports during fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>With the release, $300 million in short-term credits has been offered to Turkey for fiscal 1997, which ends September 30.</p>
<p>USDA said it did not alter the commodities eligible for the credits nor the terms for them.</p>
</text>
